      <li>Integrated debugger: Basilisk brokers debugpy through the language server (press F5). None of <a href="https://github.com/microsoft/pyright" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Pyright</a>, <a href="https://github.com/python/mypy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">mypy</a>, <a href="https://github.com/astral-sh/ty" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ty</a>, or <a href="https://github.com/facebook/pyrefly" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Pyrefly</a> documents an integrated debugger &mdash; each self-describes as a type checker and/or language server in its own repository (linked).</li>
      <li>Implementation, runtime, LSP scope, editor extensions and license for each competitor link inline to that project&rsquo;s own repository, docs, or marketplace listing: Pyright&rsquo;s language features ship via the proprietary <a href="https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=ms-python.vscode-pylance" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Pylance</a> extension; <a href="https://github.com/python/mypy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">mypy</a> is a static type checker (no first-party language server); <a href="https://github.com/astral-sh/ty" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ty</a> and <a href="https://github.com/facebook/pyrefly" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Pyrefly</a> are each a type checker and language server with an official VS Code extension.</li>
      <li>Pyrefly throughput (1.85M LOC/sec) from <a href="https://pyrefly.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">pyrefly.org</a> (measured on 166-core Meta infrastructure).</li>
      <li>Performance-benchmark table: mean wall-clock over {{ benchmarks.meta.runsCount }} hyperfine runs of each tool&rsquo;s CLI against large single-rule fixtures, measured on {{ benchmarks.meta.cpu }} ({{ benchmarks.meta.os }}, {{ benchmarks.meta.arch }}, {{ benchmarks.meta.cores }} cores) on {{ benchmarks.meta.generated }}. Tool versions: {% for t in benchmarks.meta.toolVersions %}{{ t.tool }} {{ t.version }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}. Source <code>benchmarks/status/{{ benchmarks.primary }}.csv</code>; reproduce with <code>make bench</code>. These are cold full-file runs and do not reflect warm incremental (LSP) performance.</li>
